        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r411744105-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Beautiful and emotional",
        "text": "This area is a must see of Kathmandu! I would definitely recommend getting a tour guide- we had a young lad called Reuben who had perfect English and was exceptionally knowledgable. Obviously with Kathmandu bargain hard for your price! The cremations that take place here occur frequently, be aware of this, it's highly emotional! But it really can connect you with humanity to feel so much kindness towards a stranger in grief. To see the rite of passage of another culture is also exceptionally interesting! You will also see the sadhus in their caves, and possibly women who have come to pray for help with regards to fertility. There is also a welfare area for the elderly. In all, well worth the entrance fee of one thousand rupees!",
        "review_tip": null,
