      {
        "review_id": 410966601,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r410966601-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Awestruck. Sobering.",
        "text": "Wow. Even as I try to recall all that I observed and saw at this temple site, I still can't seem to take it all in. I am not a Hindu, but I do respect everyone's religion, so I entered this site with an attitude of a \"learner\". First and foremost: if you are a \"westerner\": someone or anyone who has not grown up in a traditional \"Hindu\" or Buddhist worldview but now claim to be a \"Hindu\" or a follower of Hinduism; DO NOT claim that until you have personally come and observed the daily rituals of traditional Hindus. Don't just make something up and call it Hinduism. Come and see real Hindu worship, death rituals, ceremonies and true Hindu faith in action before you simply \"claim\" to be a Hindu (I'm looking at you, Hollywood Hipsters).\nI saw death rituals and families seeking to find peace for their loved ones who have passed on. I saw Sadhus trying to impress me with face paint and strange antics using their \"private parts\" (I can't go into more detail here). I saw women seeking \"identity\" by asking these Sadhus to help them have children. I saw people worshipping idols, gods and statues.  A mass of humanity seeking peace. I heard chants and laughter; crying and small talk. I smelled the burning of flesh and the rancid smell of sweat, trash and monkeys.  This experience is simply overwhelming.",
        "review_tip": null,
